# Changes to these paths need a code owner's approval before merge (D-042).
# Everything else auto-merges when all required checks pass.
#
# Two owners, and the second one is not decoration: GitHub does not let anyone
# approve their own pull request, and this repository's pull requests are
# opened by @bvst. With @bvst alone listed, the code-owner gate could never be
# satisfied on the work that actually happens here — it would be a rule that
# blocks everything rather than a rule that checks anything. @urso-agent is the
# owner's second account and exists for exactly this. See D-071.
/apps/server/src/domain/          @bvst @urso-agent
/apps/server/src/modules/alerts/  @bvst @urso-agent
/apps/server/src/worker.ts        @bvst @urso-agent
/apps/mobile/src/safety-core/     @bvst @urso-agent
/.github/                         @bvst @urso-agent
/.claude/                         @bvst @urso-agent
# Loaded into every agent session, and states the non-negotiables and the
# binding-decisions rule. As governance-critical as anything under /.claude/.
/CLAUDE.md                        @bvst @urso-agent
/scripts/                         @bvst @urso-agent
/package.json                     @bvst @urso-agent
/packages/contracts/released/     @bvst @urso-agent
/docs/plan/decisions.md           @bvst @urso-agent
/infra/                           @bvst @urso-agent

# Reviewer memory changes often and needs no approval (last match wins).
/.claude/agent-memory/
